1,0 $Stipe well-developed, centrally inserted $G. cerkesii
1,2 $Stipe reduced, eccentric or latéral, sometimes absent
2,0 $Pileus 5-15 mm, distinctly pigmentée!, brown or ochraceous-pink; pileipellis made up of two types of éléments; pileocystidia capitate; on old stems and lcaf-sheaths of Typha latifolia, rarely on Gares $G. menieri
2,3 $Pileus 1-5 mm broad, white to pale ochraceous; pileipellis made up of one type of elements; pileocystidia not capitatc; on différent substrata
3,0 $Lamellae absent, hymenium smooth or rarely slightly wrinkled; pileus and stipe with very slender, tapering cystidia, 60-120 x 3.0-10 pm; on leaf-sheets of Cladiwn mariscus $G. comelii
3,4 $Lamellae present; pileo- and caulocystidia never tapering into a pointed apex; on sedges (Carex spp.) in marshes and fens
4,0 $Pileus white; lamellae fold-like, often furcate; basidia 2-spored; spores ( 12) 16.5-22.5 (24.5) x (4.5) 5.0-6.5 (7.0) pm $G. caricis
4,0 $Pileus veiy pale ochraceous-pink with paler margin; lamellae usually well-developed and reaching the margin of pileus; basidia 4-spored; spores ( 11.5) 4.0-18 (22) x 4.5-6.0 (7.0) pm $G. pseudocaricis
